    {
      "name": "mplt_ABC_MAPPING_AUDIT",
      "calculation_description": "This mapplet is designed to audit mapping processes by capturing and transforming metadata related to mappings, workflows, and folders. It uses expressions and lookups to derive mapping IDs and workflow run IDs, ensuring accurate tracking and auditing of ETL processes.",
      "implementation_notes": "The mapplet consists of several transformations: \n1. **Input Transformation (int_ABC_MAPPING_AUDIT_INPUT)**: Captures metadata such as mapping name, folder name, and workflow name.\n2. **Expression Transformation (exp_ABC_MAPPING_AUDIT_ID_LOOKUP)**: Utilizes expressions to calculate mapping IDs and workflow run IDs using local variables and lookup procedures. Key expressions include:\n   - `v_RECORD_NUM + 1`\n   - `IIF(v_RECORD_NUM = 1,:LKP.lkp_MAP_ID(MAPPING_NAME, FOLDER_NAME) , v_MAPNG_ID)`\n   - `IIF(v_RECORD_NUM = 1, IIF(ISNULL(:LKP.LKP_WORKFLOW_RUN_ID_ABC(WORKFLOW_NAME)), :LKP.lkp_WORKFLOW_RUN_ID(WORKFLOW_NAME), :LKP.LKP_WORKFLOW_RUN_ID_ABC(WORKFLOW_NAME)), v_WRK_FLOW_RUN_ID)`\n3. **Output Transformation (out_ABC_MAPPING_AUDIT_OUTPUT)**: Outputs the calculated fields such as CR_BY_MAPNG_ID, DW_CR_TMSP, UPD_BY_MAPNG_ID, DW_UPD_TMSP, and WRK_FLOW_RUN_ID.\n4. **Lookup Procedures**: Includes reusable lookups like `lkp_WORKFLOW_RUN_ID`, `lkp_MAP_ID`, and `lkp_WORKFLOW_RUN_ID_ABC` to fetch IDs based on input metadata."
    },
    {
      "name": "lkp_ABC_GET_DATA_CENTER",
      "calculation_description": "This lookup procedure enriches data with the data center ID based on workflow names and retrieves the workflow run ID from the REP_WFLOW_RUN table.",
      "implementation_notes": "select (CASE WHEN workflow_name like '%LADC%' THEN 'L' WHEN workflow_name like '%OHDC%' THEN 'O' ELSE '' END) as DATA_CENTER_ID, WORKFLOW_RUN_ID as WRKFL_RUN_ID from REP_WFLOW_RUN a"
    }
  ],
