ert Else Update: NO\nUpdate Else Insert: NO\nDatetime Format: N/A\nThousand Separator: None\nDecimal Separator: .\nCase Sensitive String Comparison: NO\nNull ordering: Null Is Highest Value\nSorted Input: NO\nLookup source is static: NO\nPre-build lookup cache: Auto\nSubsecond Precision: 0\n\n- **lkp_ABC_WRKFL_CMPNT_OBJ_STG_TO_PRE_FDR_TBL_OBJ_ID_REPROC_INSERT**\n  - **Description**: This lookup procedure enriches data by retrieving specific object IDs for reprocessing from the staging to pre-final table. It ensures that only relevant records are processed further.\n  - **Logic**: Connection Information: $DBConnection_FDWS_ABC_ODBC\n\n- **lkp_WORKFLOW_RUN_ID**\n  - **Description**: This lookup procedure retrieves the WORKFLOW_RUN_ID from the WORKFLOW_NAME using a SQL override to select the maximum WORKFLOW_RUN_ID for each WORKFLOW_NAME from the REP_WFLOW_RUN table.\n  - **Logic**: SELECT MAX(WORKFLOW_RUN_ID) as WORKFLOW_RUN_ID, WORKFLOW_NAME AS WORKFLOW_NAME FROM REP_WFLOW_RUN GROUP BY WORKFLOW_NAME\n\n- **lkp_REF_PARENT_PLCY_EXP_SRC_SYS_PLCY_NUM**\n  - **Description**: Enriches policy data with source system policy number, source system code, and line of business code from the reference parent policy table.\n  - **Logic**: SELECT DISTINCT A.SRC_SYS_PLCY_NUM AS SRC_SYS_PLCY_NUM, A.SRC_SYS_CD AS SRC_SYS_CD, A.LOB_CD AS LOB_CD FROM $$FDR.REF_PARENT_PLCY_EXP A WHERE A.SRC_SYS_PLCY_NUM IN (SELECT x.POLICY_NUMBER FROM $$STG.STG_TFPLCY_TRAN_RESULT x)\n\n- **lkp_REPROC_TFPLCY_TRAN_RESULT_TFPLCY_TRAN_RESULT_SK**\n  - **Description**: Enriches transaction results with mapping IDs using a lookup procedure.\n  - **Logic**: SELECT A.TFPLCY_TRAN_RESULT_SK as TFPLCY_TRAN_RESULT_SK, A.PRE_FDR_MAPNG_ID as PRE_FDR_MAPNG_ID FROM FDWS.REPROC_TFPLCY_TRAN_RESULT A, FDWS.STG_TFPLCY_TRAN_RESULT B WHERE A.TFPLCY_TRAN_RESULT_SK = B.TFPLCY_TRAN_RESULT_SK\n\n- **lkp_FDR_FIRE_SOI_SOI_ID**\n  - **Description**: Enriches data with SOI ID from the FDR_FIRE_SOI table\n\n- **lkp_FDR_FIRE_PLCY_TRANS_RSLT_TGT_DUP_CHK_LAT_DT**\n  - **Description**: This lookup procedure enriches policy transaction results with additional attributes such as effective date and facesheet print date. It uses a SQL override to fetch data from the FDR_FIRE_PLCY_TRANS_RSLT table based on policy IDs and timestamps.\n  - **Logic**: SELECT A.PLCY_ID_SK AS PLCY_ID_SK, A.TRANS_TMSP AS TRANS_TMSP, A.EFF_DT AS EFF_DT, A.FACESHEET_PRNT_DT AS FACESHEET_PRNT_DT FROM $$FDR.FDR_FIRE_PLCY_TRANS_RSLT A WHERE A.PLCY_ID_SK IN (SELECT PLCY_ID_SK FROM $$FDR.FDR_PARENT_PLCY B WHERE B.SRC_SYS_PLCY_NUM IN (SELECT POLICY_NUMBER FROM $$STG.STG_TFPLCY_TRAN_RESULT))\n\n- **lkp_ABC_WRKFL_CMPNT_OBJ_STG_TO_PRE_FDR_COL_OBJ_ID**\n  - **Description**: This lookup procedure enriches workflow component objects by mapping target table and column names to source table and column names using a predefined SQL override.\n  - **Logic**: select a.WRKFL_CMPNT_OBJ_ID as TRGT_TBL_WRKFL_CMPNT_OBJ_ID, a.OBJ_TBL_NM as TRGT_TBL_NM, b.OBJ_TBL_NM as SRC_TBL_NM, a.OBJ_COL_NM as TRGT_COL_NM, b.OBJ_COL_NM as SRC_COL_NM from ABC.ABC_CTRL_WRKFL_CMPNT_OBJ a, ABC.ABC_CTRL_WRKFL_CMPNT_OBJ b where a.WRKFL_CMPNT_SRC_OBJ_ID = b.WRKFL_CMPNT_OBJ_ID and a.WRKFL_OBJ_TYP_CD = 'C'\n\n- **lkp_FDR_FIRE_PLCY_DEPENDENT_PLCY_ID_SK**\n  - **Description**: Enriches policy data by looking up dependent policy IDs from multiple sources.\n  - **Logic**: SELECT PLCY_ID_SK as PLCY_ID_SK, CEA_PLCY_ID_SK as CEA_PLCY_ID_SK FROM (SELECT PLCY_ID_SK as PLCY_ID_SK, CEA_PLCY_ID_SK as CEA_PLCY_ID_SK FROM FDR.FDR_FIRE_PLCY_DEPENDENT a, STG.STG_TFPLCY_TRAN_RESULT b where a.DEPNDNT_PLCY_NUM = b.POLICY_NUMBER UNION SELECT PLCY_ID_SK as PLCY_ID_SK, CEA_PLCY_ID_SK as CEA_PLCY_ID_SK FROM FDR.PRE_FDR_FIRE_PLCY_DEPENDENT c, STG.STG_TFPLCY_TRAN_RESULT d where c.DEPNDNT_PLCY_NUM = d.POLICY_NUMBER) BB ORDER BY CEA_PLCY_ID_SK\n\n- **lkp_FDR_FIRE_PLCY_TRANS_RSLT_TGT_DUP_CHK_APLD_DT**\n  - **Description**: Enriches policy transactions with additional details from the FDR_FIRE_PLCY_TRANS_RSLT table using a lookup procedure.\n  - **Logic**: SELECT A.PLCY_ID_SK AS PLCY_ID_SK, A.TRANS_TMSP AS TRANS_TMSP, A.EFF_DT AS EFF_DT, A.FACESHEET_PRNT_DT AS FACESHEET_PRNT_DT FROM $$FDR.FDR_FIRE_PLCY_TRANS_RSLT A WHERE A.PLCY_ID_SK IN (SELECT PLCY_ID_SK FROM $$FDR.FDR_PARENT_PLCY B WHERE B.SRC_SYS_PLCY_NUM IN (SELECT POLICY_NUMBER FROM $$STG.STG_TFPLCY_TRAN_RESULT))\n\n- **lkp_FDR_FIRE_PLCY_TRANS_RSLT_LOW_EXP**\n  - **Description**: This lookup procedure enriches policy transactions with effective and transaction timestamps from the FDR_FIRE_PLCY_TRANS_RSLT table, using specific conditions to filter the data.\n  - **Logic**: SELECT A.PLCY_ID_SK as PLCY_ID_SK, A.TRANS_TMSP as TRANS_TMSP, A.EFF_DT as EFF_DT, A.END_EFF_DT as END_EFF_DT FROM FDR.FDR_FIRE_PLCY_TRANS_RSLT A WHERE A.END_EFF_DT='01-01-1800'\n\n- **mplt_LOG_ABC_ERROR_MESSAGES**\n  - **Description**: This Re-Usable Mapplet Logs/Writes Error Messages To The ABC_CTRL_SYS_MSG Table. Every Record Sent To the REPROC Tables Should Log the Reason Why It Was Sent To Reprocessing.\n  - **Logic**: The mapplet consists of several transformations including an Update Strategy for inserting error records, an Expression transformation for assigning error IDs and values, and various Lookup Procedures to derive keys. It processes input fields such as workflow names and component names, and outputs fields like error descriptions and timestamps.\n\n- **lkp_FDR_FIRE_PROP_STRUCTURE_MAJOR_SOI_ID_TRNS_RSLT**\n  - **Description**: This lookup procedure enriches the transformation process by retrieving policy and source system information based on specific conditions. It uses a complex SQL override to fetch data from multiple tables, ensuring that the correct policy identifiers are matched and returned.\n  - **Logic**: SELECT X.SOI_ID as SOI_ID, X.PLCY_ID_SK as PLCY_ID_SK, X.SRC_SYS_CD as SRC_SYS_CD FROM ((SELECT A.SOI_ID as SOI_ID, A.PLCY_ID_SK as PLCY_ID_SK, CASE WHEN A.SRC_SYS_CD='AFL' THEN 'FL' WHEN A.SRC_SYS_CD='AFO' THEN 'FO' ELSE A.SRC_SYS_CD END as SRC_SYS_CD FROM $$FDR.FDR_FIRE_PROP_STRUCTURE A WHERE A.PLCY_ID_SK in (SELECT coalesce(CP.PLCY_ID_SK, AA.PLCY_ID_SK) FROM (select PP.PLCY_ID_SK from $$FDR.FDR_PARENT_PLCY PP where PP.SRC_SYS_PLCY_NUM in (select POLICY_NUMBER from $$STG.STG_TFPLCY_TRAN_RESULT) and PP.LOB_CD = 'F') AA LEFT OUTER JOIN $$FDR.FDR_FIRE_PLCY_DEPENDENT CP ON AA.PLCY_ID_SK = CP.CEA_PLCY_ID_SK union SELECT coalesce(CP.PLCY_ID_SK, AA.PLCY_ID_SK) FROM (select PP.PLCY_ID_SK from $$FDR.PRE_FDR_PARENT_PLCY PP where PP.SRC_SYS_PLCY_NUM in (select POLICY_NUMBER from $$STG.STG_TFPLCY_TRAN_RESULT) and PP.LOB_CD = 'F') AA LEFT OUTER JOIN $$FDR.PRE_FDR_FIRE_PLCY_DEPENDENT CP ON AA.PLCY_ID_SK = CP.CEA_PLCY_ID_SK ) UNION SELECT B.SOI_ID as SOI_ID, B.PLCY_ID_SK as PLCY_ID_SK, CASE WHEN B.SRC_SYS_CD='AFL' THEN 'FL' WHEN B.SRC_SYS_CD='AFO' THEN 'FO' ELSE B.SRC_SYS_CD END as SRC_SYS_CD FROM $$FDR.PRE_FDR_FIRE_PROP_STRUCTURE B WHERE B.PLCY_ID_SK in (SELECT coalesce(CP.PLCY_ID_SK, AA.PLCY_ID_SK) FROM (select PP.PLCY_ID_SK from $$FDR.FDR_PARENT_PLCY PP where PP.SRC_SYS_PLCY_NUM in (select POLICY_NUMBER from $$STG.STG_TFPLCY_TRAN_RESULT) and PP.LOB_CD = 'F') AA LEFT OUTER JOIN $$FDR.FDR_FIRE_PLCY_DEPENDENT CP ON AA.PLCY_ID_SK = CP.CEA_PLCY_ID_SK UNION SELECT coalesce(CP.PLCY_ID_SK, AA.PLCY_ID_SK) FROM (select PP.PLCY_ID_SK from $$FDR.PRE_FDR_PARENT_PLCY PP where PP.SRC_SYS_PLCY_NUM in (select POLICY_NUMBER from $$STG.STG_TFPLCY_TRAN_RESULT) and PP.LOB_CD = 'F') AA LEFT OUTER JOIN $$FDR.PRE_FDR_FIRE_PLCY_DEPENDENT CP ON AA.PLCY_ID_SK = CP.CEA_PLCY_ID_SK))) AS X UNION SELECT X.SOI_ID as SOI_ID, X.PLCY_ID_SK as PLCY_ID_SK, X.SRC_SYS_CD as SRC_SYS_CD FROM ((SELECT A.SOI_ID as SOI_ID, A.PLCY_ID_SK as PLCY_ID_SK, A.SRC_SYS_CD as SRC_SYS_CD FROM $$FDR.FDR_FIRE_SOI_MBLHM A WHERE A.PLCY_ID_SK in (SELECT coalesce(CP.PLCY_ID_SK, AA.PLCY_ID_SK) FROM (select PP.PLCY_ID_SK from $$FDR.FDR_PARENT_PLCY PP where PP.SRC_SYS_PLCY_NUM in (select POLICY_NUMBER from $$STG.STG_TFPLCY_TRAN_RESULT) and PP.LOB_CD = 'F') AA LEFT OUTER JOIN $$FDR.FDR_FIRE_PLCY_DEPENDENT CP ON AA.PLCY_ID_SK = CP.CEA_PLCY_ID_SK union SELECT coalesce(CP.PLCY_ID_SK, AA.PLCY_ID_SK) FROM (select PP.PLCY_ID_SK from $$FDR.PRE_FDR_PARENT_PLCY PP where PP.SRC_SYS_PLCY_NUM in (select POLICY_NUMBER from $$STG.STG_TFPLCY_TRAN_RESULT) and PP.LOB_CD = 'F') AA LEFT OUTER JOIN $$FDR.PRE_FDR_FIRE_PLCY_DEPENDENT CP ON AA.PLCY_ID_SK = CP.CEA_PLCY_ID_SK) UNION SELECT B.SOI_ID as SOI_ID, B.PLCY_ID_SK as PLCY_ID_SK, B.SRC_SYS_CD as SRC_SYS_CD FROM $$FDR.PRE_FDR_FIRE_SOI_MBLHM B WHERE B.PLCY_ID_SK in (SELECT coalesce(CP.PLCY_ID_SK, AA.PLCY_ID_SK) FROM (select PP.PLCY_ID_SK from $$FDR.FDR_PARENT_PLCY PP where PP.SRC_SYS_PLCY_NUM in (select POLICY_NUMBER from $$STG.STG_TFPLCY_TRAN_RESULT) and PP.LOB_CD = 'F') AA LEFT OUTER JOIN $$FDR.FDR_FIRE_PLCY_DEPENDENT CP ON AA.PLCY_ID_SK = CP.CEA_PLCY_ID_SK UNION SELECT coalesce(CP.PLCY_ID_SK, AA.PLCY_ID_SK) FROM (select PP.PLCY_ID_SK from $$FDR.PRE_FDR_PARENT_PLCY PP where PP.SRC_SYS_PLCY_NUM in (select POLICY_NUMBER from $$STG.STG_TFPLCY_TRAN_RESULT) and PP.LOB_CD = 'F') AA LEFT OUTER JOIN $$FDR.PRE_FDR_FIRE_PLCY_DEPENDENT CP ON AA.PLCY_ID_SK = CP.CEA_PLCY_ID_SK))) AS X\n\n- **lkp_FDR_FIRE_PLCY_TRANS_RSLT_MIN_EFF_DT**\n  - **Description**: This lookup will help calculate min_eff_dt.\n  - **Logic**: SELECT a.PLCY_ID_SK as PLCY_ID_SK, MIN(a.EFF_DT) as EFF_DT FROM FDR.FDR_FIRE_PLCY_TRANS_RSLT a GROUP BY a.PLCY_ID_SK\n\n- **lkp_WORKFLOW_RUN_ID_ABC**\n  - **Description**: This lookup procedure retrieves the WORKFLOW_RUN_ID from the ABC_AUDIT_WRKFL_RUN table based on the current workflow name. It uses a SQL override to fetch the maximum WORKFLOW_RUN_ID for workflows that are currently running.\n  - **Logic**: SELECT WRKFL_NM AS WORKFLOW_NAME, MAX(WRKFL_RUN_ID) AS WORKFLOW_RUN_ID FROM ABC.ABC_AUDIT_WRKFL_RUN R, ABC.ABC_CTRL_WRKFL_PRMTR P WHERE P.WRKFL_NM ='$PMWorkflowName' AND R.WRKFL_ID = P.WRKFL_ID AND WRKFL_STAT='Running' GROUP BY WRKFL_NM\n\n- **mplt_FDR_LIB_LOG_ABC_ERROR_MESSAGES.lkp_FDR_LIB_STD_MSG_ID**\n  - **Description**: This lookup procedure retrieves the standard message ID (STD_MSG_ID) from the ABC_CTRL_SYS_STD_MSGS table based on the system message code (SYS_MSG_CD). It uses a caching mechanism to optimize performance and applies a condition to match SYS_MSG_CD with i_SYS_MSG_CD.\n  - **Logic**: Lookup table: ABC_CTRL_SYS_STD_MSGS\nLookup condition: SYS_MSG_CD = i_SYS_MSG_CD\nConnection Information: $DBConnection_FDWS_ABC_ODBC\nLookup caching enabled: YES\nLookup policy on multiple match: Use First Value\nRecache if Stale: NO\nTracing Level: Normal\nLookup cache directory name: $PMCacheDir\nLookup cache initialize: NO\nLookup cache persistent: NO\nLookup Data Cache Size: Auto\nLookup Index Cache Size: Auto\nDynamic Lookup Cache: NO\nSynchronize Dynamic Cache: NO\nOutput Old Value On Update: NO\nUpdate Dynamic Cache Condition: TRUE\nCache File Name Prefix: \nRe-cache from lookup source: NO\nInsert Else Update: NO\nUpdate Else Insert: NO\nDatetime Format: \nThousand Separator: None\nDecimal Separator: .\nCase Sensitive String Comparison: NO\nNull ordering: Null Is Highest Value\nSorted Input: NO\nLookup source is static: NO\nPre-build lookup cache: Auto\nSubsecond Precision: 0\n\n- **mplt_ABC_MAPPING_AUDIT**\n  - **Description**: This mapplet is designed to audit mapping processes by capturing and transforming metadata related to mappings, workflows, and folders. It uses expressions and lookups to derive mapping IDs and workflow run IDs, ensuring accurate tracking and auditing of ETL processes.\n  - **Logic**: The mapplet consists of several transformations: \n1. **Input Transformation (int_ABC_MAPPING_AUDIT_INPUT)**: Captures metadata such as mapping name, folder name, and workflow name.\n2. **Expression Transformation (exp_ABC_MAPPING_AUDIT_ID_LOOKUP)**: Utilizes expressions to calculate mapping IDs and workflow run IDs using local variables and lookup procedures. Key expressions include:\n   - `v_RECORD_NUM + 1`\n   - `IIF(v_RECORD_NUM = 1,:LKP.lkp_MAP_ID(MAPPING_NAME, FOLDER_NAME) , v_MAPNG_ID)`\n   - `IIF(v_RECORD_NUM = 1, IIF(ISNULL(:LKP.LKP_WORKFLOW_RUN_ID_ABC(WORKFLOW_NAME)), :LKP.lkp_WORKFLOW_RUN_ID(WORKFLOW_NAME), :LKP.LKP_WORKFLOW_RUN_ID_ABC(WORKFLOW_NAME)), v_WRK_FLOW_RUN_ID)`\n3. **Output Transformation (out_ABC_MAPPING_AUDIT_OUTPUT)**: Outputs the calculated fields such as CR_BY_MAPNG_ID, DW_CR_TMSP, UPD_BY_MAPNG_ID, DW_UPD_TMSP, and WRK_FLOW_RUN_ID.\n4. **Lookup Procedures**: Includes reusable lookups like `lkp_WORKFLOW_RUN_ID`, `lkp_MAP_ID`, and `lkp_WORKFLOW_RUN_ID_ABC` to fetch IDs based on input metadata.\n\n- **lkp_ABC_GET_DATA_CENTER**\n  - **Description**: This lookup procedure enriches data with the data center ID based on workflow names and retrieves the workflow run ID from the REP_WFLOW_RUN table.\n  - **Logic**: select (CASE WHEN workflow_name like '%LADC%' THEN 'L' WHEN workflow_name like '%OHDC%' THEN 'O' ELSE '' END) as DATA_CENTER_ID, WORKFLOW_RUN_ID as WRKFL_RUN_ID from REP_WFLOW_RUN a\n\n4. **Targets**\n\n- **ABC_GATE_KPR**\n  - **Description**: Target table in Snowflake for storing gatekeeper data.\n  - **Connection details**: SnowflakeCloudDataWarehouse\n\n- **ABC_BAL_ROW_COUNTS**\n  - **Description**: Stores row count metrics for various workflow components in Snowflake.\n  - **Connection details**: SnowflakeCloudDataWarehouse\n\n- **ABC_BAL_DETAIL_AMTS**\n  - **Description**: Stores balance detail amounts with associated workflow component object IDs.\n  - **Connection details**: SnowflakeCloudDataWarehouse\n\n- **ABC_CTRL_WRKFL_CMPNT_OBJ**\n  - **Description**: Target table in Snowflake for workflow component objects.\n  - **Connection details**: SnowflakeCloudDataWarehouse\n\n- **ABC_CTRL_SYS_MSG**\n  - **Description**: Stores system messages related to workflow components in Snowflake.\n  - **Connection details**: SnowflakeCloudDataWarehouse\n\n- **REPROC_TFPLCY_TRAN_RESULT**\n  - **Description**: Stores transaction results for policy reprocessing in Snowflake.\n  - **Connection details**: SnowflakeCloudDataWarehouse\n\n- **PRE_FDR_FIRE_PLCY_TRANS_RSLT**\n  - **Description**: Stores transformed policy transaction results in Snowflake for further analysis and reporting.\n  - **Connection details**: SnowflakeCloudDataWarehouse\n\n- **FDR_FIRE_PLCY_TRANS_RSLT**\n  - **Description**: Stores transformed policy transaction results in Snowflake for further analysis and reporting.\n  - **Connection details**: SnowflakeCloudDataWarehouse\n"
